# Repo & workspace safety

## Single source of truth

- Treat `C:\Users\r_she\Documents\fatigue-app-latest` as the **only** workspace root for this project.
- Treat `app-next/` as the **current app** (Next.js + Prisma + NextAuth). Do not switch stacks or folders unless the user explicitly asks.

## Do not “move the repo”

Never do any of the following unless the user explicitly requests it in the current message:

- Create a new project folder (e.g. by cloning again, copying, extracting zips into a new name).
- Rename the repo folder, relocate it, or recommend using a different folder as the “main” one without verifying `.git` and explaining why.
- Change Git remotes (`git remote add/set-url/remove`), switch SSH↔HTTPS, or “fix casing” of the remote URL.
- Push to a different remote, different repo, or different default branch.

## Git actions require explicit permission

- Do not run `git commit`, `git push`, or any destructive git commands unless the user explicitly asks.
- If git output indicates multiple folders exist, **stop** and determine which folder contains `.git` before continuing.

